## E. The tool proves it can fail

$ python3 03-verify_run_record.py --self-test

FAIL  prefix collision is a difference               got e41eba7f89729c8300000000..., manifest says e41eba7f89729c8358da8b98...

self-test: 0 passed, 1 failed (1 failed means the checker compares all 64)


The self-test compares a digest against the same digest with its last 48 characters replaced. It
expects exactly one failure and exits 0 only when it gets one, so a future edit that quietly
restores prefix comparison makes the suite red rather than green.

The comparison method now reads:

    def compare(self, label: str, got, want) -> None:
        if got == want:
            ...

The short forms in the log are display only. Nothing on the decision path is truncated.
